ents the rate of outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission in each state and reporting area for the years 2009-2013. Of the 52 reporting sites, four reported <10 outbreaks each, 24 reported 10-99 outbreaks each, and 24 reported >100 outbreaks each.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":503,"renderedHeight":373,"naturalWidth":503,"naturalHeight":373,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 395 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":34479},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f2.gif","alt":"This figure is a histogram that presents the number of outbreak reports and median state reporting rate (per million population) of outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission for each year for the years 2009-2013. A total of 10,756 outbreaks were reported to NORS during the 5-year period.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":495,"renderedHeight":432,"naturalWidth":495,"naturalHeight":432,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 384 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":34542},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f3.gif","alt":"This figure is a bar stacked graph that presents the percentage of outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission, by suspected or confirmed etiology in the United States, for the years 2009-2013. Of the 10,756 AGE outbreaks primarily transmitted through person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission, 7,370 (69%) had a single suspected or confirmed etiology, 3,326 (31%) had an unknown etiology, and 60 (<1%) had multiple etiologies.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":500,"renderedHeight":454,"naturalWidth":500,"naturalHeight":454,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 567 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":22276},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f4.gif","alt":"This figure is a stacked bar graph that presents the percentage of outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission, by confirmed etiology in the United States, for the years 2009-2013. Of the 4,112 outbreaks with at least one laboratory-confirmed etiology, norovirus was the most common etiology, reported in 86% (n = 2,888) of 3,362 outbreaks transmitted through person-to-person contact or environmental contamination and 44% (n = 327) of 750 of those outbreaks with unknown transmission mode.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":502,"renderedHeight":456,"naturalWidth":502,"naturalHeight":456,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 585 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":25383},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f5.gif","alt":"This figure is a stacked bar graph that presents the number of outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission. This information is conveyed by month of first onset of illness and suspected or confirmed etiology in the United States, for the years 2009-2013. Outbreaks were more frequent during the winter as 5,716 (53%) of the 10,756 outbreaks occurred during December-February.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":844,"renderedHeight":534,"naturalWidth":844,"naturalHeight":534,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 469 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":31655},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f6.gif","alt":"This figure is a stacked bar graph that presents the percentage of cases in outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission, by sex and suspected or confirmed etiology in the United States, for the years 2009-2013. Among the 6,099 outbreaks with information on distribution of cases by sex, 66% of cases occurred in females.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":842,"renderedHeight":560,"naturalWidth":842,"naturalHeight":560,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 414 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":46817},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6412a1f7.gif","alt":"This figure is a bar graph that presents to percentage of cases in outbreaks of acute gastroenteritis transmitted by person-to-person contact, environmental contamination, and unknown mode of transmission, distributed by age group and by suspected or confirmed etiology, in the United States, for the years 2009-2013. Among the 5,405 outbreaks with information on age distribution of cases, 12% of cases occurred in children aged <10 years, 21% of cases occurred in adolescents and adults aged 10-49 years, 49% of cases occurred in adults aged >49 years, and 18% of cases were of unknown age.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":831,"renderedHeight":556,"naturalWidth":831,"naturalHeight":556,"loading"